<article class="env-lemma" id="06PC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06PC">Lemma <span data-tag="06PC">78.26.2</span>.</a> Assume $B \to S$ and $(U, R, s, t, c)$ as in Definition <a href="/tag/044Q" data-tag="044Q">78.20.1</a> (1). Let $G/U$ be the stabilizer group algebraic space of the groupoid $(U, R, s, t, c, e, i)$, see Definition <a href="/tag/0448" data-tag="0448">78.16.2</a>. There is a canonical $2$-cartesian diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathcal{S}_ G \ar[r] \ar[d] &  \mathcal{S}_ U \ar[d] \\  \mathcal{I}_{[U/R]} \ar[r] &  [U/R] }  \]
</div>
  <p> of stacks in groupoids of $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/04ZN" data-tag="04ZN">78.25.3</a> it suffices to prove that the morphism $s' : R' \to G$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/06PB" data-tag="06PB">78.26.1</a> isomorphic to the base change of $s$ by the structure morphism $G \to U$. This base change property is clear from the construction of $s'$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>